IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `act-ch13-structure`
IMPORT `act-ch15-aids`
IMPORT `act-seat`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory) -- worked cases for the seat layer.
-- One case at least for every question in act-seat.l4, then cases outside the encoding.
-- Every expected value is written from the section named beside it, before the run; none is copied from a run.
-- Dates are written Date day month year. The weekdays used: 10 March 2025 is a Monday; 8 April 2026 is a Wednesday, 10 April 2026 a Friday, 11 April 2026 a Saturday.

§ `Cases: the questions of a person with a time limit`

§§ `When an Act or instrument that affects me begins`

-- s 73 (1) (a): an Act that says nothing about its start begins on the day after its notification day.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act begin` (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS Date 11 3 2025
-- s 73 (1) (b): an Act that provides a different date begins on that date.
#ASSERT `On which day does an Act begin` (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 7 2025) EQUALS Date 1 7 2025

-- s 73 (2) (a): a legislative instrument that says nothing begins on the day after its notification day.
#ASSERT `On which day does a legislative instrument begin` (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) `an Act` EQUALS Date 11 3 2025
-- s 73 (2) (b): a later date provided by the instrument is the day it begins.
#ASSERT `On which day does a legislative instrument begin` (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 7 2025) `the instrument, without authority given by an Act` EQUALS Date 1 7 2025
-- s 73 (2) (c): an earlier date provided by an Act is the day it begins.
#ASSERT `On which day does a legislative instrument begin` (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) `an Act` EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- s 73 (2) (d): an earlier date provided by the instrument under authority given by an Act is the day it begins.
#ASSERT `On which day does a legislative instrument begin` (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) `the instrument, under authority given by an Act` EQUALS Date 1 3 2025
-- s 73 (3): an earlier date provided by the instrument without authority does not apply; it begins on the day after its notification day.
#ASSERT `On which day does a legislative instrument begin` (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) `the instrument, without authority given by an Act` EQUALS Date 11 3 2025

-- s 73 (4) (a): an instrument that is not a legislative instrument begins on the day after it is made.
#ASSERT `On which day does an instrument that is not a legislative instrument begin` (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) `an Act` EQUALS Date 11 3 2025
-- s 73 (4) (a): where it must be approved, on the day after it is approved.
#ASSERT `On which day does an instrument that is not a legislative instrument begin` (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) `an Act` EQUALS Date 15 3 2025
-- s 73 (4) (b): a later date provided by the instrument is the day it begins.
#ASSERT `On which day does an instrument that is not a legislative instrument begin` (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 7 2025) `the instrument, without authority given by an Act` EQUALS Date 1 7 2025
-- s 73 (4): an earlier date the instrument provides without authority does not apply.
#ASSERT `On which day does an instrument that is not a legislative instrument begin` (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 1 3 2025) `the instrument, without authority given by an Act` EQUALS Date 11 3 2025

-- s 75A (1): a law commences retrospectively if it commences earlier than the day after its notification day.
#ASSERT `Does a law begin before the day it was notified` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 1 3 2025)
#ASSERT `Does a law begin before the day it was notified` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`Does a law begin before the day it was notified` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 11 3 2025))

-- s 77 (2): a commencement notice may fix a day later than its notification day, and the law begins on it.
#ASSERT `On which day does a law begin under a commencement notice` (Date 1 7 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS Date 1 7 2025
-- s 77 (3): a day on or before the notice's notification day: the law begins on the day after it.
#ASSERT `On which day does a law begin under a commencement notice` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS Date 11 3 2025
#ASSERT `On which day does a law begin under a commencement notice` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS Date 11 3 2025
-- s 77 (4): where the notice clearly indicates the earlier date under authority given by an Act, the earlier date stands.
#ASSERT `On which day does a law begin under a commencement notice` (Date 1 3 2025) (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS Date 1 3 2025

-- s 79 (1): a postponed law not begun within 6 months beginning on its notification day begins on the first day after that period.
#ASSERT `On which day does a postponed law begin by itself` (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 9 2025)
-- s 79 (1) does not say what happens to a law that has begun within the 6 months.
#ASSERT `On which day does a postponed law begin by itself` (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `When a law that affects me ends`

-- s 85 (3): a law not remade on the day it is repealed continues until the end of the day, and the repeal takes effect at midnight on the day.
#ASSERT `On which day does the repeal of a law take effect` (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)
-- s 85 (2): a law remade on the day it is repealed: the repeal takes effect when the remade law commences.
#ASSERT `On which day does the repeal of a law take effect` (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE TRUE (Date 11 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2025)
-- s 85 (2) does not say when the repeal takes effect if the remade law's commencement is not stated.
#ASSERT `On which day does the repeal of a law take effect` (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 89 (1) (a): an amending law is repealed on the day after all its provisions have commenced.
#ASSERT `On which day is an amending law repealed by itself` TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2025)
-- s 89 (1) (b): or on the day after the last provisions that have not commenced are omitted or cannot commence.
#ASSERT `On which day is an amending law repealed by itself` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 21 3 2025)
-- s 89 (1): where both are true the amending law is repealed on the day after the earlier.
#ASSERT `On which day is an amending law repealed by itself` TRUE (Date 10 3 2025) TRUE (Date 20 3 2025) EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2025)
-- s 89 (1) does not say when an amending law is repealed if neither has happened.
#ASSERT `On which day is an amending law repealed by itself` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 89 (2): an appropriation Act for the financial year beginning on 1 July 2025 is repealed on the last day of that year, 30 June 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day is an appropriation Act repealed by itself` 2025 EQUALS Date 30 6 2026

§§ `Ages and periods of time`

-- s 149: a person is an age in years at the beginning of the birthday for the age.
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 15 1 2000) (Date 14 1 2025) EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 15 1 2000) (Date 15 1 2025) EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 15 1 2000) (Date 1 1 1999) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day do I reach a given age` (Date 15 1 2000) 18 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 1 2018)

-- s 151 (2), table 151: item 1 includes the stated day; item 2 does not; item 4 does not.
#ASSERT `Is the day my period is counted from or to part of the period` `beginning at, on or with a stated day`
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the day my period is counted from or to part of the period` `beginning from or after a stated day`)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the day my period is counted from or to part of the period` `ending before a stated day`)
-- s 151 (3): despite item 2, a thing that may be done within a period after a stated day may be done on the stated day.
#ASSERT `May I act on the day my period is counted from` `beginning from or after a stated day` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I act on the day my period is counted from` `beginning from or after a stated day` FALSE)

-- s 151 (1), (2), table 151 item 2: a period of 30 days from or after 1 January 2026 begins on 2 January and ends on 31 January 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 30 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- the dictionary meaning of month: 2 months from 31 December 2025 end on 28 February 2026 (no corresponding day of February).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 2 months `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 12 2025) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- the dictionary meaning of month: one month from 31 January 2024 begins on 1 February 2024 and ends immediately before 1 March, on 29 February 2024 (a leap year; compare the dictionary's example 2).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 1 months `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 1 2024) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- s 6: a law that says expressly that this Act's counting does not apply displaces s 151 (a determinative provision), so the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 30 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 6 (2): a contrary intention that is not manifest does not displace a determinative provision of a law made after 1 January 2006.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 30 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- s 6 (3): for a law made on or before 1 January 2006 the provision is not determinative, so a contrary intention that is not manifest displaces it.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 30 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2004) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 151A (4) (b): for anything else, a day that is not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday is a working day.
#ASSERT `Is a day a working day for what I must do` (Date 10 4 2026) `anything else` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a day a working day for what I must do` (Date 11 4 2026) `anything else` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000))
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a day a working day for what I must do` (Date 10 4 2026) `anything else` TRUE (Date 10 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000))
-- s 151A (4) (a): for something at an office, a day when the office is open; a day listed as closed is not one.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a day a working day for what I must do` (Date 10 4 2026) `something at an office of a public entity` TRUE (Date 10 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000))
#ASSERT `Is a day a working day for what I must do` (Date 10 4 2026) `something at an office of a public entity` TRUE (Date 11 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)
-- s 151A (4) (b) (iii): for something by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution, a day it observes as a bank holiday is not a working day.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is a day a working day for what I must do` (Date 10 4 2026) `anything else, by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution` TRUE (Date 10 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000))
#ASSERT `Is a day a working day for what I must do` (Date 10 4 2026) `anything else, by or in relation to an authorised deposit-taking institution` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000)

-- s 151A (2): 3 days from or after Wednesday 8 April 2026 end on Saturday 11 April; the thing may be done on Monday 13 April.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` 3 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 8 4 2026) `anything else` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 13 4 2026)
-- s 151A (4) (b) (ii): with Monday 13 April a public holiday, the next working day is Tuesday 14 April.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` 3 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 8 4 2026) `anything else` TRUE (Date 13 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 14 4 2026)
-- s 151A (4) (a): at an office closed on Saturday 11 and Sunday 12 April, the thing may be done on Monday 13 April.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` 3 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 8 4 2026) `something at an office of a public entity` TRUE (Date 11 4 2026) TRUE (Date 12 4 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 13 4 2026)
-- s 151A (1): where the last day is a working day it is not moved: 2 days from or after Wednesday 8 April end on Friday 10 April.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` 2 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 8 4 2026) `anything else` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 4 2026)
-- s 151 (1), table 151 and the dictionary meaning of month: 2 months from 31 December 2025 end on Saturday 28 February 2026; the thing may be done on Monday 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` 2 months `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 31 12 2025) `anything else` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
-- s 6: a law that says expressly that this Act's counting does not apply displaces s 151A, so the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` 3 days `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 8 4 2026) `anything else` FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) (Date 1 6 2020) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 151 (2), table 151, item 5: a notice of motion to be served 2 days before the return date, a Friday (10 April 2026), is served on or before the Tuesday (7 April 2026).
#ASSERT `What is the latest day for the earlier event` 2 (Date 10 4 2026) EQUALS Date 7 4 2026
#ASSERT `How many days lie between 2 events` (Date 7 4 2026) (Date 10 4 2026) EQUALS 2

-- s 151B: a thing for which no time is fixed must or may be done as soon as possible and as often as needed.
#ASSERT `When must I do something for which the law sets no time` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `as soon as possible and as often as needed`
#ASSERT `When must I do something for which the law sets no time` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 151C (2): a person may apply for the time to be extended even though it has ended, where a court can extend it; s 151C (5): only for an applicable law.
#ASSERT `May I ask for more time even though my time has ended` (Date 1 6 2010) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I ask for more time even though my time has ended` (Date 1 6 2010) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I ask for more time even though my time has ended` (Date 1 6 2004) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 152: the obligation to do an act continues until the act is done.
#ASSERT `Must I still do what the law requires after the time for it has passed` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I still do what the law requires after the time for it has passed` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must I still do what the law requires after the time for it has passed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Fines I must pay`

-- s 133 (1), (2): 20 penalty units is $3 200 for an individual (a unit is $160) and $16 200 for a corporation (a unit is $810).
#ASSERT `How much is a fine expressed in penalty units, in dollars` `an Act` `an individual` TRUE 20 EQUALS JUST 3200
#ASSERT `How much is a fine expressed in penalty units, in dollars` `an Act` `a corporation` TRUE 20 EQUALS JUST 16200
#ASSERT `How much is a fine expressed in penalty units, in dollars` `a subordinate law` `a corporation` TRUE 0.5 EQUALS JUST 405
-- s 133 (1): a penalty not expressed in penalty units is not covered; s 133 (2): an offender that is neither an individual nor a corporation is not covered.
#ASSERT `How much is a fine expressed in penalty units, in dollars` `an Act` `an individual` FALSE 20 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `How much is a fine expressed in penalty units, in dollars` `an Act` `an offender who is neither an individual nor a corporation` TRUE 20 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 161 (3) (a) to (f): the most a corporation can be fined where the penalty is imprisonment only, by the length of the imprisonment.
#ASSERT `What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment` TRUE TRUE 6 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment` TRUE TRUE 7 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment` TRUE TRUE 12 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment` TRUE TRUE 24 EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment` TRUE TRUE 60 EQUALS JUST 500
#ASSERT `What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment` TRUE TRUE 120 EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment` TRUE TRUE 121 EQUALS JUST 1500
#ASSERT `What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment` FALSE TRUE 6 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Documents served on me`

-- s 250 (1): a document served by post is taken to be served when it would have been delivered in the ordinary course of post.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to be served` `by sending it by prepaid post` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2025)
-- s 250 (3), (4): a document sent by email is presumed served when sent if the equipment gave no failure signal and no doubt is raised.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to be served` `by email` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)
-- s 250 (3): where the equipment indicated a failure the presumption does not apply, and the Act does not say when the document is served.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to be served` `by email` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 250 (3): evidence sufficient to raise doubt removes the presumption.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to be served` `by fax` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 250 (5): a document left at an address as the sections provide is taken to be served when it was left.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to be served` `by leaving it at an address with someone there` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 10 3 2025)

§§ `Cases outside the encoding`

-- Three years from 16 July 2025: the text defines a year as a calendar year and has no rule for a period of years that does not start on 1 January, so the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 3 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 16 7 2025) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- One year from 29 February 2024: the same.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 1 years `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 29 2 2024) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period counted in weeks: the text defines no week as a unit of a period, so the Act does not answer.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` 2 weeks `beginning from or after a stated day` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 6 2020) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A person born on 29 February, asked their age on 28 February in a year that has no 29 February: the text does not say which day is their birthday.
#ASSERT `How old am I on a given day` (Date 29 2 2000) (Date 28 2 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day do I reach a given age` (Date 29 2 2000) 1 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A document served by giving it to the person: s 250 says nothing about when that is taken to be served.
#ASSERT `On which day am I taken to be served` `by giving it to the person, or to an executive officer` (Date 10 3 2025) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
